  "note": "Training code is fit of scripts/train_xgb.py and train_one of scripts/train_gru.py, unchanged, with --storm-weight K set per configuration (oculstorm.metrics.storm_weights: weight rises linearly from 1 at Dst >= 0 nT to K at Dst <= -100 nT). All other options are the production defaults. As in the scripts, early stopping uses the validation set with the same K weights, so validation RMSE is slightly optimistic for every configuration alike. Grid K in 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 10 for each family; K = 1 is the current production configuration and reproduces models/xgb_dst_1h.ubj and models/gru_dst_1h_seed0.pt exactly on validation. XGBoost is deterministic (random_state 0), so one fit per K. GRU: seed 0 per K, then the 3 configurations with the lowest seed 0 storm MSE among those within +1% overall MSE of production seed 0 re-run with seeds 1 and 2. XGBoost fits used n_jobs 3, GRU torch threads 3. Validation RMSE and MSE are unweighted, reported for all hours and per regime by the observed Dst at the target hour (quiet Dst > -50 nT, storm Dst <= -50 nT, intense Dst <= -100 nT). Bootstrap: paired moving block bootstrap (oculstorm.metrics.block_bootstrap_rmse, 168 hour blocks, 2000 resamples, seed 0) of the relative MSE change against production.",
